# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Several guard tests (e.g. app/src/settings_view/mod_tests.rs,
# app/src/castcodes_public_surface_tests.rs) `include_str!` Rust sources
# and assert on multi-line substrings whose expected text embeds `\n`.
# Without forcing LF, Windows checks these files out as CRLF (git's
# `core.autocrlf` default on the hosted runners), so the embedded `\n`
# no longer matches the file's `\r\n` and the tests fail on Windows only
# (see #193). Check out Rust sources with LF on every platform.
*.rs text eol=lf

*.pdb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
input_classifier/models/* filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
input_classifier/models/**/*tokenizer.json linguist-generated=true
